2) The aha type is too uniform. The "what to leave unbuilt" idea (L32, L46, L50, L75) and the "forecast reading" idea are the freshest, and each appears only a few times.
3) Difficulty. The late third averages roughly 55-65% casual, which is on target. Several finales sit at 47-55% casual with skilled at 67-83% (L102, L110, L112, L120). L120 at 55/67 is a spike for a gentle send-off. L90 and L102 are close to the edge.
4) Some mid-game levels have no trap hidden in them. L19, L55, L79, L103 and L115 are real breathers. L37, L61 and L63 are fine.
5) Too many levels hinge on one fixed number: "27 vs 36 seats". Players will learn to count hops and ignore the board.
